me><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>KANZAKI SUSUMU</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>MATSUDA MASATOSHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>NAGAI TAKAYUKI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>NOMURA TAKAO</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>OHKAWA KENICHI</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><last-name>SHIMOJO MORIYASU</last-name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>IWAI, HISAYUKI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>KANZAKI, SUSUMU</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>MATSUDA, MASATOSHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NAGAI, TAKAYUKI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>NOMURA, TAKAO</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>OHKAWA, KENICHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>SHIMOJO, MORIYASU</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A thermoplastic composition which is obtained by melt-kneading (1) 55 to 75 wt.% crystalline polypropylene resin together with (2) 10 to 30 wt.% elastomer comprising either a rubber containing a vinylaromatic compound or a mixture thereof with an ethylene/ alpha -olefin random copolymer rubber and (3) 15 to 25 wt.% talc having an average particle diameter of 3  mu m or smaller. The composition satisfies specific requirements with respect to: the long period obtained by X-ray small-angle scattering attributable to the vinylaromatic-containing rubber in a blend obtained by melt-kneading the ingredients (1) and (2); the shape and diameter of the elastomer particles present near the polypropylene/elastomer interface in the blend; and the difference between the glass transition point of the ingredient (1) and that of the composition attributable to the crystalline polypropylene homopolymer parts. The composition has a satisfactory balance between impact resistance and rigidity and has excellent injection moldability.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une composition thermoplastique obtenue par pétrissage par fusion (1) de 55 à 75 % en poids de résine de polypropylène cristalline conjointement avec (2) 10 à 30 % en poids d'élastomère comprenant, soit un caoutchouc contenant un composé vinylaromatique ou un mélange de celui-ci avec un caoutchouc copolymère aléatoire éthylénique/ alpha -oléfinique et (3) 15 à 25 % en poids de talc possédant un diamètre de particule moyen de 3  mu m ou moins. Ladite composition remplit des conditions spécifiques relatives à : la longue période obtenue par la dispersion à petit angle de rayons X, attribuée au caoutchouc contenant un composé vinylaromatique dans un mélange obtenu par pétrissage par fusion des ingrédients (1) et (2) ; la forme et le diamètre des particules élastomères présentes à proximité de l'interface polypropylène/élastomère dans le mélange ; et la différence entre la température de transition vitreuse de l'ingrédient (1) et celle de la composition, attribuée aux parties d'homopolymère polypropylénique cristallin. Ladite composition se caractérise par un équilibre satisfaisant entre la résistance aux chocs et la rigidité et présente une excellente aptitude au moulage par injection.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>